2026-05-03 10:13:30,582 [INFO] [TC 1] Model Answer : King Pandukabhaya was the ruler who laid the foundation stone for the construction of Anurapura. He was the founder of the first capital in the history of Sri Lanka. The historical significance of this event lies in the fact that it marked the beginning of a centralized political system in the country. The establishment of a capital city facilitated the administration of the kingdom, the collection of taxes, and the maintenance of law and order. It also led to the development of agriculture, trade, and culture, laying the foundation for the growth of a prosperous and organized society. The creation of a permanent capital helped to establish a sense of national identity and unity among the people. In addition, it enabled the rulers to implement policies for the protection of the environment and the conservation of natural resources, as seen in the inscriptions of King Mihinthu IV and King Udayya III. The foundation of the capital at Anurādhapura became an important milestone in the political, economic, and social development of ancient Sri Lanka, shaping the course of the country's history for centuries to come.
